    "tranche": "T6",
    "tranche_reason": "The study evaluates the composability of SAE-selected feature sets in vision-language models, a new modality and setting. It does not test dictionary-size splitting or the specific split and absorption claims listed here.",
    "gate_note": "The study trains one fixed-size TopK SAE and tests interventions on Pattern and Global feature sets and their union. These results bear on feature-set composability, but the study does not compare SAE dictionary sizes or test whether parent features split into children. Rows below record the related composability results as none of the listed versions.",
    "test_reason": "The study trains one fixed-size TopK SAE (32,768 latents, k=32) on Qwen3-VL-8B layer 21 and tests steering and ablation of selected feature sets and their union. It has no dictionary-size comparison, no parent/child or feature-family analysis, no absorption measure and no comparison of training objectives. The SAE is a tool for its composability question, not a test of feature splitting. The record's 'tests'/T3 is wrong: no row bears on any version, which the record itself concedes.",
    "authors_conclusion": "Broadly correct. The authors conclude that individually steering a task-selective SAE feature set modestly helps accuracy, but additive union steering degrades accuracy and raises output drift. They attribute this to geometric antagonism (negative cosine) amplified via LayerNorm noise, most robustly at layer 21 of Qwen3-VL-8B. Note that the Pattern gain is not uniform: InternVL3.5-8B is -1.30 pp and SNLI-VE is -0.33 pp.",
    "recipe": "different",
    "recipe_differences": "The study trains a fixed-size TopK SAE and intervenes on selected Pattern, Global, and Union sets in VLMs; it does not use a dictionary-size sweep or the feature-matching and partition measurements needed to test splitting.",
    "method_sensitivity": "The reported outcome varies across datasets and model families. The study also reports layer and intervention-scale sensitivity, but those sweeps do not test dictionary-size splitting.",
    "fits_no_version": [
      {
        "finding": "Pattern-set steering gives small accuracy gains in most models and datasets. The norm-matched Union of Pattern and Global sets lowers accuracy and raises output drift. The two sets' mean updates have cosine -0.33, and 45% of cross-set pairs are negatively aligned.",
        "proposed_claim": "Task-selective SAE feature sets in VLMs can be individually steerable yet interfere under additive composition.",
